IMPORT prelude

-- Victoria Theatre Act 1903 (Singapore) -- who holds the Theatre and for what (s 2(1)), which uses the Government may permit a person
-- or company to make of it (s 2(1)), refusal without reasons (s 2(2)), and the exemption from the Public Entertainments Act 1958 (s 3).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/VTA1903.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; it annotates no
-- later amendment. The retrieval record calls it the current version as at 01 Oct 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0253 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act has three sections, and the whole operative text (ss 2 and 3) is encoded. Not encoded: s 1 (short
-- title), and the preamble's history of the Old Town Hall, the lost trust deed and the Victoria Memorial Hall fund, except to tell
-- the Memorial Hall apart from the Theatre. What terms and conditions the Government sets, and what follows a breach of them, the
-- Act does not say and this row does not guess.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victoria Theatre Act 1903 -- nouns`

-- The preamble distinguishes the Old Town Hall, to be "converted into a public Theatre", from "The Victoria Memorial Hall" built on
-- another portion of the same land. Only the Theatre is named in ss 2 and 3.
DECLARE Venue IS ONE OF
    `the Victoria Theatre`
    `the Victoria Memorial Hall`
    `another venue`

-- The uses a person or company may be permitted to make of the Theatre, and some it does not list. Whether a private business
-- meeting, an exhibition or a shop counts as an "entertainment ... or otherwise" is a reading: this row treats them as outside the
-- list (an inference, not a statement of the text).
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `a public stage play`
    `a private stage play`
    `a public theatrical entertainment`
    `a private entertainment that is not theatrical`
    `a concert`
    `a public meeting`
    `a private business meeting`
    `a trade exhibition`
    `a retail shop`

§§ `2(1) -- the trust and the uses the Government may permit`

-- s 2(1): "The Government shall hold the Victoria Theatre upon trust to use it for such public purposes as it thinks fit, and from
-- time to time, at its discretion, and upon such terms and conditions as it thinks fit, to permit any person or company to use it for
-- the public or private representation of stage plays or the holding of public or private entertainments, theatrical or otherwise,
-- concerts or public meetings."
--
-- "public or private" qualifies stage plays and entertainments; "public" qualifies meetings. Concerts are unqualified.
GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is one the Government may permit` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `a private business meeting` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a trade exhibition` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a retail shop` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The Government's own use is confined to "public purposes as it thinks fit".
GIVEN `the purpose is public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may itself use the Theatre for the purpose` IF
    `the purpose is public`

-- A person or company uses the Theatre only by the Government's permission ("to permit any person or company"), and only for a use
-- of the listed kinds. The text gives no route to use without permission.
GIVEN `the use` IS A Use, `the Government has permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person or company may use the Theatre for it` IF
    `the use is one the Government may permit` `the use` AND `the Government has permitted it`

§§ `2(2) -- refusal without reasons`

-- s 2(2): "The Government may refuse any application made for the use of the Theatre without assigning any reason for its refusal."
-- "any application" includes one for a use of the listed kinds. Nothing in the Act gives an applicant a right to be granted use.
GIVEN `the use` IS A Use, `reasons were given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may refuse the application` IF
    TRUE

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is entitled to be granted use` IF
    FALSE

§§ `3 -- exemption from the Public Entertainments Act 1958`

-- s 3: "The Victoria Theatre shall be exempt from the operation of the Public Entertainments Act 1958."
-- The exemption names the Theatre only, not the Memorial Hall. Whether the 1958 Act applies to any other venue is for that Act.
GIVEN `the venue` IS A Venue
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act exempts the venue from the Public Entertainments Act 1958` IF
    CONSIDER `the venue`
    WHEN `the Victoria Theatre` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
